From: PowerPhone research platform <powerphone@csr460.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Separate qualified per-target capture and playback contracts

Preserve the existing Frankel PCM rates, geometry, queues, endpoint identities,
readiness and mixer behavior behind its exact vendor-device identity. Separate
capture from playback rate/geometry so a future target need not share one rate.
Reserve Cubs-specific addresses but leave its backend unimplemented and rates
zero: it must not advertise ports, touch Frankel mixer controls or register an
unqualified module. No Cubs product, RC, VINTF or stock-HAL change is included.

This delta was extracted against a separate reconstruction of patches0001-0028,
not a broad diff of the populated AOSP worktree.

